\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 This brief proposes piloting 
\f0\b Scenario Immersion Protocol (SIP)
\f1\b0  - an experiential training methodology that addresses persistent engagement challenges in prevention education. Rather than transmitting information through lectures or content, SIP creates structured experiences where service members discover their own behavioral patterns around peer intervention, help-seeking, and prevention topics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The approach:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 60-minute facilitated scenario experience with 4-6 participants\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Participants take anonymous roles in prevention-relevant scenarios\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Guided choice-making reveals actual behavioral patterns\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Structured debrief connects insights to real behavior change\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Pilot scope:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 2-4 week timeline\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 3 IPPW partners\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ~8 hours Briefs Studio support per IPPW\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Zero new budget (uses existing consulting allocation)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 If successful:
\f1\b0  Scalable methodology for prevention training that actually changes behavior, not just knowledge.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 THE PROBLEM\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Current prevention training approaches aren't working:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Service members disengage from PowerPoint lectures and video content\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Information is transmitted but behavior doesn't change\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 IPPWs report low participation and Command deprioritization\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prevention metrics remain stagnant despite educational efforts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The root issue:
\f1\b0  Standard training assumes a knowledge deficit - if people just 
\f2\i knew
\f1\i0  the right thing to do, they'd do it. But behavior change doesn't work that way. Service members already know they should intervene when a buddy is struggling. They know substance abuse is harmful. They know help-seeking is important.\

\f0\b Knowledge isn't the barrier. The actual barriers are:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Social pressure and peer dynamics\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fear of consequences or judgment\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Uncertainty about how to intervene effectively\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Disconnect between what people think they'd do and what they actually do\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These barriers operate at the level of instinct and social conditioning - not information processing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 THE SOLUTION: SCENARIO IMMERSION PROTOCOL\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 SIP creates conditions where participants can safely explore their actual behavioral patterns without performance pressure. By placing people in realistic scenarios with genuine choices, we reveal the current "set point" - what people actually do versus what they think they should do.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 How it works:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 1. STORY CAPTURE (60 minutes)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Briefs Studio facilitates a conversation with the IPPW to understand:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Specific prevention challenges at their installation\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Local culture and dynamics\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Barriers to intervention and help-seeking\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Previous approaches and what hasn't worked\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This session is recorded and transcribed (consistent with previous Story Capture methodology).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. CUSTOM PROTOCOL DEVELOPMENT (3-4 hours)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Using the Story Capture conversation, Briefs Studio creates:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Custom scenario
\f1\b0  tailored to that installation's context\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 4-6 choice points
\f1\b0  with three options each (spanning proactive, neutral, avoidant responses)\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Narrative map
\f1\b0  showing decision trees and consequences\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Facilitation guide
\f1\b0  with prompts and debrief questions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. FACILITATOR TRAINING (60-90 minutes)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Briefs Studio trains the IPPW on facilitation approach:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How to hold psychological safety\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Presenting choices without judgment\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Navigating the decision tree\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Facilitating meaningful debrief\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. SESSION EXECUTION (60 minutes)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 IPPW facilitates experience with 4-6 service members:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Setup (5 min):
\f1\b0  Frame the experience, assign anonymous roles\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Scenario play (30 min):
\f1\b0  Participants navigate 4-6 choice points as their characters\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Debrief (25 min):
\f1\b0  Structured reflection on patterns observed\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 5. ITERATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Based on results, refine protocol and scale to additional IPPWs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

