\f0\b \cf0 The mechanism:
\f1\b0  By creating 
\f0\b controlled fragmentation
\f1\b0  - temporary separation from identity and social expectation through anonymous roles - participants can explore actual behavioral patterns. The debrief makes these patterns visible, which is the moment they become editable.\
This is similar to how the military uses After Action Reviews (AARs) - observe what actually happened, reflect on why, adjust future behavior. SIP creates a safe space to observe behavioral patterns before they have real-world consequences.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 THEORETICAL FOUNDATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 SIP is based on 
\f0\b Sleepy Planet Protocol
\f1\b0  - a collaborative imagination methodology I've been developing for several years as part of my Briefs Studio practice. Sleepy Planet uses guided scenario exploration to reveal subconscious patterns and enable psychological insight.\
The underlying principle: humans have behavioral "set points" (default patterns) shaped by environment, culture, and social conditioning. To change behavior, you need to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Make the current set point visible\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Create conditions where alternative patterns can be explored safely\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Allow conscious observation of what emerges\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 SIP adapts this methodology specifically for prevention contexts, using group dynamics and role-based scenarios rather than individual imagination work.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

