\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 RISKS & MITIGATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Risk: Facilitation quality varies, experience falls flat
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Mitigation:
\f1\i0  Co-facilitation model ensures quality in pilot phase. Develop structured facilitation guides with decision trees so IPPWs have clear framework. Continue refinement based on results.\

\f0\b Risk: Service members see this as "touchy-feely" and resist
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Mitigation:
\f1\i0  Frame as tactical scenario training (familiar military concept). Use anonymous roles to reduce vulnerability. Emphasize voluntary participation and psychological safety.\

\f0\b Risk: Difficult to measure behavior change in short timeline
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Mitigation:
\f1\i0  Focus pilot success metrics on engagement and insight quality (measurable immediately). Document anecdotal behavior changes. Long-term impact assessment can follow if pilot succeeds.\

\f0\b Risk: Scenarios not relevant to specific installation contexts
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Mitigation:
\f1\i0  Story Capture process ensures customization. Each protocol built from actual IPPW experience and local challenges. IPPWs review scenarios before facilitation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
